WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:55.890
<b>Departing Shortly</b>

3
00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.520
<b>Blue Station Entrance
Shipyard Island</b>

4
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.470
All right, CP9 should be here any second
now.

5
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.570
Let's go, Robin.

6
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.470
You'll have to get on that train sooner or
later.

7
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.870
You heard me.

8
00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.380
Take the lady and
get moving, you dimwits.

9
00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.840
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

10
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.470
A government rep,
a bunch of marines and Robin.

11
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.240
Let's see, how should I play this?

12
00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.240
Because inside of me,

13
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.210
I carry a darkness that none of you know about.

14
00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.620
No matter how you look at it,

15
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.380
they're obviously
escorting her away.

16
00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.650
But those guys are chumps,
if she wanted to run,

17
00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.520
she could take
them out, no problem.

18
00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.230
She must be planning something we don't
know about.

19
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.970
There's gotta be a reason why she's not
running.

20
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.570
I'm here for you my darling!

21
00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.610
Oh, my prince has
come to rescue me!

22
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.580
I've been waiting!

23
00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.350
Aw, you want me
to save you, Robin?

24
00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.360
Corgy, sir. CP9 is here.

25
00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.060
Stop man handling me, damn it!

26
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.360
This body is expensive!

27
00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.040
Oh man that's Rob Lucci, huh?

28
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.000
He's got the eyes of a killer!

29
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.270
Never thought I'd
see CP9 in person.

30
00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.110
I'm gonna give you
to the count of ten,

31
00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.510
and then it's gonna
get ugly! Do you hear me?!

32
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.150
Let go!

33
00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.620
You don't know who you're messing with!

34
00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.990
I've got eight thousand men
hiding in the shadows

35
00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.300
just waiting to teach
you losers a lesson!

36
00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.530
Yep! They're gonna pop
out any minute now!

37
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.470
Any minute, you hear me?!

38
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.570
Better put me down quick!

39
00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.010
All right, I'll give
you one last chance!

40
00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.110
Excellent work as
always, sirs and madam!

41
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.150
Here, Mr. Lucci, your coat.

42
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.750
What is this, a parade?

43
00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:21.660
Stop it.

44
00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.280
It's foolish.

45
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.680
Ah, right.

46
00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.370
Sorry, sir!

47
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.720
This isn't over until we reach
Enies Lobby, so look sharp!

48
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.920
Everyone, board the
sea train immediately!

49
00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.020
You heard the man!

50
00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.320
Get on the train and make it quick!

51
00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:40.630
Hey, you bastards
gonna put me down or...?!

52
00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.030
Who are those
guys in the suits?

53
00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.730
He says he's sorry for
causing us so much trouble

54
00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.700
then he goes and gets
in trouble all over again.

55
00:04:54.730 --> 00:05:01.160
<b>Ruins of the Galley-La Company HQ</b>

56
00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.190
A little further to the right!

57
00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.500
Spray over there!

58
00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.500
Bring the hose this way!

59
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.120
So you mean Robin
doesn't hate us after all?!

60
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.800
Uh-huh!

61
00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.630
I'm so happy!

62
00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.040
Huh? He's a raccoon dog?

63
00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.870
I thought he was a reindeer!

64
00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.110
Did he just transform, or what?

65
00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.150
Anyway Chopper.

66
00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.040
We have to find the rest
of the crew right away

67
00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.870
so we can all go rescue Robin!

68
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.740
Okay! Let's go!

69
00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.340
Uh, but where are they?

70
00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:23.910
I don't know!

71
00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.150
That's why we have to find them!

72
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.850
Yeah! Let's do this!

73
00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.350
Now he's a gorilla!

74
00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.890
Wait, you two.

75
00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.440
I don't care if you
go after Nico Robin

76
00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.830
but before you run off, you
should know that the sea train

77
00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:45.370
for government personnel is
departing at 11 o'clock tonight.

78
00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.900
This is just my guess

79
00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.140
but there's a good chance
you'll find CP9 there.

80
00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:54.610
And that means Nico Robin will be there as
well.

81
00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:55.880
Thanks to Aqua Laguna,

82
00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.820
they're stopping all service
after this final departure.

83
00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.880
In other words,

84
00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.680
you won't be able to chase
them on another train.

85
00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.820
Wait, you mean we have to...

86
00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.920
Since you obviously
can't sail in this weather,

87
00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.430
you won't be able to
leave the island

88
00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.100
unless you go after
that train right now.

89
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:12.650
Huh?!

90
00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:13.210
No way!

91
00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.280
What time is it?

92
00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.250
Almost 10:30.

93
00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.410
What?!

94
00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.350
That means we've only got half an hour
left!

95
00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.140
Hey, but you're the mayor, right?

96
00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.240
Can't you do something to stop the train?

97
00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.750
Mwell unfortunately,
it's bound for Enies Lobby,

98
00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.250
which is only accessible
to government personnel.

99
00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.650
Even the engine driver works for the
government.

100
00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.670
So I have no say in this matter.

101
00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.240
Oh no!

102
00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:36.970
I guess our only choice
is to head to the station

103
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.110
and try to talk
some sense into Robin.

104
00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.340
Chopper!

105
00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.280
I'll tell you which direction
Luffy and Zoro flew off in,

106
00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.210
so you go search there, okay?

107
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.350
If you find them,

108
00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.200
tell them to come to the
station as quickly as they can!

109
00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:48.930
Okay.

110
00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.910
Got it!

111
00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.040
Hey, listen up.

112
00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:53.980
Look you guys!

113
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.370
Paulie's okay!

114
00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.420
See that girl over there?

115
00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.900
I want you to help her find her buddies.

116
00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.030
What?

117
00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.270
You sure that smoke didn't
get to your brain, Paulie?

118
00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.530
These are the guys that
tried to kill Mister Iceburg.

119
00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.000
We should wring their
no-good-sorry necks!

120
00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.540
Besides, why should we waste
our time helping some criminals

121
00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.980
when Lucci and Kaku
are still missing?!

122
00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:15.240
The Straw Hats aren't the ones who did it,
okay?

123
00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.260
The real criminals set them up!

124
00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.720
If we hadn't been so damn blind,

125
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.720
we wouldn't be in this
situation right now!

126
00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.820
I don't know the real identity
of those guys in the masks

127
00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.300
but I do know
that the Straw Hats

128
00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:28.260
tried to protect us from them.

129
00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.220
As a matter of fact, Iceburg
and I wouldn't even be alive

130
00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.730
right now if it
wasn't for their help.

131
00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:41.270
Don't bother looking for
Lucci and Kaku there's no point.

132
00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.310
In fact, I don't know if we'll ever be
seeing them again.

133
00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.170
What?

134
00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.880
If you know what
happened to the foremen,

135
00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.210
then you gotta tell us, Paulie!

136
00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.530
They went back home.

137
00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.510
Huh?!

138
00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.210
Why would they do
that at a time like this?!

139
00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.480
Just shut up and go find Straw Hat!

140
00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.150
Hey, immoral girl!

141
00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.950
What? You're still
calling me that?

142
00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.380
If you're going to the station,
I'll show you the way.

143
00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.750
Uh thanks, I guess.

144
00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.970
Hey, hold a sec, Paulie!

145
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.900
Is that stuff you told us true?!

146
00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.650
Quit yer yapping and
help them out already!

147
00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.590
You're making Galley-La look bad!

148
00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.560
Yes!

149
00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:15.630
Sorry, sir!

150
00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:16.560
We'll do our best!

151
00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.380
You're the boss!

152
00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.020
Yeah!

153
00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.820
We'll help any way we can!

154
00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:20.960
Open the cage!

155
00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.120
Bring out the yagaras!

156
00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.420
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

157
00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:29.180
"Went back home," did they?

158
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.230
I spared 'em the details.

159
00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.900
It's better that way.

160
00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.970
It was bad enough when we found out.

161
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.800
They deserve the truth but
I don't wanna hurt those guys.

162
00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.380
Hey!

163
00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.090
Guys!

164
00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.290
Hello?

165
00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.930
Hey! Guys! Can you hear me?!

166
00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.360
Luffy!

167
00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.160
Zoro!

168
00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.190
Sanji!

169
00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.370
Usopp, you can come with us too,
okay?

170
00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.130
Now shout it with me!

171
00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:10.200
All right buddy, you
got it. Let's do it, guys!

172
00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.900
Yeah!

173
00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.500
Hey!

174
00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.530
Luffy!

175
00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.870
Zoro!

176
00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.240
Sanji!

177
00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:18.580
Usopp,

178
00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.380
you can come with us too.

179
00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.150
Take that canal over
on the left-hand side.

180
00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:31.160
It's a shortcut to the station!

181
00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.440
We still have 20 minutes
before the train leaves.

182
00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.840
Don't go, Robin.

183
00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.350
You don't have to sacrifice yourself!

184
00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.820
We can save you!

185
00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:54.550
Mr. Yagara, you think you can
go a little bit faster, please?

186
00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.270
The 11 o' clock train
is about to depart.

187
00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:11.970
All passengers going from
Blue Station to Enies Lobby,

188
00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.950
please board immediately.

189
00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.510
That hurt!

190
00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.240
I don't wanna hear another
word out of you two!

191
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.610
Well maybe I wouldn't
complain so much

192
00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:23.420
if you weren't
such big jerkwads!

193
00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.950
Yeah you big jerkwads!

194
00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.350
Why don't you come
over here and fight?!

195
00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:28.590
Hey, that's too much.

196
00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.610
Due to the approaching storm
surge, the departure time

197
00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.640
has been moved up and the
train will be departing shortly.

198
00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.010
Damn it, this was
bad enough already.

199
00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:42.920
After all these years,

200
00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.220
our mission has
finally come to an end.

201
00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.490
We're not there yet.

202
00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:47.500
Stop spouting nonsense

203
00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.860
and take your mission
seriously, you fool.

204
00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.700
My apologies.

205
00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.320
You can't sail in this weather.

206
00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.880
Unless you can catch that train,
you won't be able to leave.

207
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.240
Come on.

208
00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.810
We're so close!

209
00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:19.490
Franky, wherever you
are I hope you're safe.

210
00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:29.760
Hey, Luffy!

211
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.630
Roronoa!

212
00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.800
Luffy!

213
00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:33.570
Hey!

214
00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.540
Come back!

215
00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.500
Where are you?!

216
00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:38.240
Come on!

217
00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.910
There's not much time!

218
00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.190
Zoro!

219
00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.340
Sanji!

220
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.880
Usopp, you can come too.

221
00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.140
Luffy, please!

222
00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:51.950
Those guys're gonna
take Robin away!

223
00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.780
We need your help!

224
00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.450
Where are you?!

225
00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:08.320
I wonder how the rest of the
crew is dealing with this mess.

226
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.590
Anyway, time's up. They'll
have to catch me later.

227
00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:16.230
I repeat: the final train will
be departing ahead of schedule.

228
00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.190
Please board immediately.

229
00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.810
Damn it!

230
00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.300
You bastards!

231
00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.810
I'm coming for you!

232
00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.070
Just wait, you'll see!

233
00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.940
Once I get out of here.

234
00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:40.960
One little slip-up,
then this crap happens.

235
00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.150
I'm coming for you bastards.

236
00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.550
Once I get out of here.

237
00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.750
Luffy!

238
00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.050
Zoro!

239
00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.540
Sanji!

240
00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.080
Where are you?

241
00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.580
We gotta save Robin!

242
00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:07.480
Straw Hat!

243
00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.070
Roronoa!

244
00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.870
I don't get it.
Where in the heck are they?

245
00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.410
Have we checked over there yet?

246
00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.820
Hey!

247
00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.240
Straw Hat!

248
00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.450
Zoro!

249
00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.170
I guess they're not here.

250
00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.700
Has anybody checked
over in the backstreets yet?

251
00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.040
I don't know if we can.

252
00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.380
They're probably completely flooded by
now.

253
00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.440
It'd be too dangerous to look for them
there.

254
00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:34.710
Come on, guys!

255
00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.050
Where are you?!

256
00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.850
There's no time!

257
00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:45.930
Excuse me.

258
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.700
The waves are getting
dangerously high,

259
00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.300
so we've decided to depart
early as a safety measure.

260
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.900
If it's any trouble, we could...

261
00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.670
It's fine.

262
00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:53.400
Just go.

263
00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.300
Coo coo!

264
00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:56.240
Yes, sir.

265
00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.610
We lived here for five years

266
00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:05.080
but even as we leave I don't
feel nostalgic in the least.

267
00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.540
Hey, was that a
steam whistle just now?

268
00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.540
If it was, that means
the train is running

269
00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.810
nearly fifteen minutes
ahead of schedule.

270
00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.750
They're probably
taking off early,

271
00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.920
'cause the weather's
getting bad.

272
00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:35.450
The government runs that line,

273
00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.790
so they can leave
whenever they want!

274
00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:39.720
Hurry it up, guys!

275
00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:41.060
The station's right there!

276
00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:43.540
Hold on, train!

277
00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.640
Don't leave yet!

278
00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.970
Attention, tonight's final
departure, heading from

279
00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:54.710
Water Seven to Enies Lobby
is now leaving the station.

280
00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:58.250
You heard her.

281
00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.680
Sit down already.

282
00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.650
Have a safe trip.

283
00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.940
I wanted nothing more than to die at that
very moment.

284
00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.220
But you forced me to live.

285
00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.160
That's your crime.

286
00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.460
I'm afraid there's no place left for me to
go or return to.

287
00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.490
So I've decided to stay here with you.

288
00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:24.320
I see your problem,

289
00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.430
guess there's no
other choice, is there?

290
00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.400
Welcome.

291
00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.800
– Luffy!
– Luffy!

292
00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:30.630
Hey, there's nothing to worry about.

293
00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.120
She isn't a bad person.

294
00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.600
Trust me, okay?!

295
00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.130
Hey, I think we're moving.

296
00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.760
Stupid government jerkwads.

297
00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.940
Good job, Mr. Yagara!

298
00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:03.110
Go down the stairs through the middle
entrance!

299
00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.070
Got it!

300
00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.680
We're coming for you
Robin, please don't go!

301
00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:14.970
Hey, stop!

302
00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:17.730
Who are you?

303
00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:18.630
That's dangerous!

304
00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.030
Stay back!

305
00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.970
Robin, get off that train!

306
00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.930
I don't care who you're
up against. We'll help you!

307
00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:32.260
Luffy!

308
00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.640
Zoro!

309
00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.180
Where are you guys?!

310
00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.890
Can't move.

311
00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.150
Wait!

312
00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.660
No!

313
00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.730
Come back!

314
00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.340
Robin!

315
00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.720
Wait!

316
00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.320
Robin!

317
00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.070
Looks like we were too late.

318
00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:38.750
Ow!

319
00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:39.660
Seriously!

320
00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:42.520
What was that guy
trying to pull, anyway?

321
00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:45.360
Whatever the case, it really doesn't
matter.

322
00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:46.460
That was a Government train.

323
00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.600
He'll be captured, and
that will be the end of it.

324
00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.770
Hey, isn't he with Galley-La?

325
00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.480
Hey, Paulie!

326
00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.040
Try to act professional, will ya?

327
00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:04.390
It looks like there's something going on
between them.

328
00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:05.760
This is a train station!

329
00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.960
People say hello and
goodbye here every day!

330
00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.660
It's our responsibility
as employees here

331
00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.700
to silently oversee
things like this.

332
00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.300
Yeah, you're right!

333
00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:17.970
Keep quiet!

334
00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:18.670
Got it?

335
00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:21.080
Quiet. Got it.

336
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.250
Train left a little early, huh?

337
00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.290
Uh, yes! That's right!

338
00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:28.360
All of the passengers
were already on board,

339
00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:29.460
so they decided to...

340
00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.460
The weather's getting
rougher by the minute, too.

341
00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.470
At this rate, Aqua Laguna could hit at any
moment!

342
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.100
With all of these factors
in mind, it was decided

343
00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:40.520
that the departure time
should be pushed forward!

344
00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.320
It's not safe here right now.

345
00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.290
You should take shelter
on the Shipbuilding Island

346
00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.540
as soon as possible.

347
00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.370
Yeah, you're right.

348
00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.310
Hey listen, the train's gone.

349
00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.280
There's nothing we can do to stop it.

350
00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.320
I hate to say it,

351
00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.520
but Enies Lobby isn't the
kind of place where...

352
00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.540
Are you crying?

353
00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.960
Hey, look I-I understand
how you must feel, but...

354
00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.050
After them!

355
00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.120
She's pissed!

356
00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:12.350
I'll never forgive those
World Government idiots!

357
00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:14.020
Listen, I need a ship!

358
00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:15.710
What in the hell are you talking about?

359
00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.580
The strongest and fastest you've got!

360
00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.400
You wanna set sail in
the middle of all this?

361
00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.990
Don't be an idiot!

362
00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:24.830
Do you have any idea how dangerous this
storm is?

363
00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:25.260
Lay off!

364
00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.360
I can handle it!

365
00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.500
Look, this isn't some
regular run-of-the-mill storm

366
00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:29.960
we're talking about!

367
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.470
It's about to be hell at sea around here!

368
00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:34.330
It's impossible to sail out now!

369
00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.560
Doing so is nothing short of a death wish!

370
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.830
Listen to me!

371
00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:41.170
Robin is throwing her life away
for our sake and I'm not gonna...

372
00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.620
That was close.

373
00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.620
Thank you!

374
00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.690
Yes, thank you!

375
00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:17.390
You saved us all!

376
00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.660
If it wasn't for you,

377
00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:21.860
we would've all been
swept out into the sea!

378
00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.120
Look at that.

379
00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:26.660
That huge fixture with the train schedule
on it was torn apart.

380
00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.800
Nothing like that has ever happened here
before.

381
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.100
Not even with Aqua Laguna.

382
00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:36.930
This thing's power is unbelievable.

383
00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:40.100
And the actual storm
isn't even here yet!

384
00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:42.840
Aqua Laguna is different this year.

385
00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.570
These waves are coming in fast!

386
00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:51.210
Hey, is that sea train that they took
Robin on in any danger?

387
00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.520
It should be able to make
it out of this rough patch

388
00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.190
before the actual
storm makes landfall.

389
00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:57.920
Unless it takes a direct hit,

390
00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:02.120
that train's capable of cutting
through these big waves.

391
00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.790
Um, excuse me.

392
00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.840
Are you Nami?

393
00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:05.660
Huh?

394
00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:06.760
Yes?

395
00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.190
Someone left you a note out in front of
the station.

396
00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.720
Must've been one
of your crewmates.

397
00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:12.310
A note?

398
00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.410
From who?

399
00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:17.020
And how did you manage to notice something
so small?

400
00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:18.160
It was right here.

401
00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.730
Whoever it was made it easy for us.

402
00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:26.760
<b>Nami, please</b>
<b>read this!</b>

403
00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:26.760
<b>If you're not Nami, 
don't. Dumbass.</b>

404
00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.840
That dimwit!

405
00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.890
So, what does it say?

406
00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.380
Give me a second.

407
00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:35.260
The first half is just a hopeless love
letter.

408
00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.330
Did she say "love letter"?

409
00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.360
It seems there's a love triangle going on
here.

410
00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.030
No.

411
00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:42.030
Considering the situation,

412
00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:44.630
I'd say the other
man is most likely...

413
00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.010
What are you staring at?

414
00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.710
The important part starts here.

415
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.580
P.S. I saw Robin get on
the 11 o'clock train.

416
00:21:57.610 --> 00:22:01.680
I'm gonna hop on board and follow her.

417
00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:03.800
Sanji got on board that train?

418
00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:06.770
Usopp's there, too?

419
00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:10.800
"And some arrogant thug with
a ducktail." Who's that?

420
00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:12.300
That must be Franky.

421
00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:13.950
Yeah, must be.

422
00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:15.770
She mentioned another man!

423
00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.310
And it sounds like Franky, of
all people, must be the fifth!

424
00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:21.580
Poor Paulie doesn't stand a chance.

425
00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:24.410
Maybe it'd be better if he just threw in
the towel.

426
00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:26.410
What in the hell
is with you guys?!

427
00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.360
Oh, and there's something else.

428
00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:31.230
This was left on the ground alongside that
letter.

429
00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:36.700
There should be at least
one transponder snail

430
00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:38.240
somewhere on that sea train.

431
00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:40.380
I'll contact you as soon as I can.

432
00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:46.840
Keep this portable one close to you at all
times, my darling.

433
00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:47.890
Just pretend it's me

434
00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:50.720
and hold it lovingly against
your soft, beautiful...

435
00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:51.710
I get it.

436
00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.180
He left this one to communicate with us.

437
00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:56.850
<b>If you're not Nami, 
don't. Dumbass.</b>

438
00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:55.180
Wow.

439
00:22:55.210 --> 00:22:58.050
He must have anticipated Nico Robin's
movements.

440
00:22:56.850 --> 00:23:00.270
<b>If you're not Nami, 
don't. Dumbass.</b>

441
00:22:58.080 --> 00:22:59.250
Pretty impressive!

442
00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.980
I'll say!

443
00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:06.160
At least for the time being, Robin has
Sanji with her.

444
00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:07.820
The rest of us will
just have to catch up

445
00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:10.180
with them at Enies Lobby.

446
00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:25.110
Man, can't even manage to light up a
single smoke out here.

447
00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.300
Really?

448
00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:30.010
So after that, Sanji went to the train
station?

449
00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:30.760
Yep!

450
00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:35.050
And Usopp's on
the train with him!

451
00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:36.810
Thank goodness!

452
00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:39.300
At any rate, no matter how
we're going to follow them,

453
00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:42.300
we can't do anything until
we find Luffy and Zoro first!

454
00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:43.240
Understand?

455
00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:43.700
Right!

456
00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:44.870
I got it Nami.

457
00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:46.970
I'm a hundred percent certain
about which way they flew

458
00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:49.760
so head in that direction
and start looking!

459
00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:51.240
You guys help look, too!

460
00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:52.800
Let's do this!

461
00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:53.870
Are you with me?

462
00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:55.770
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

463
00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:58.040
We won't let you down!

464
00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:10.320
Now, what would be the best way

465
00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:12.990
for one to sneak
inside this thing?

466
00:24:14.290 --> 00:24:15.090
Whoa!

467
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:17.120
This storm is insane!

468
00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:26.200
Collier Shoot!

469
00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.280
Who in the hell are you?

470
00:24:35.790 --> 00:24:36.960
Hey, hold it!

471
00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:39.710
Where do you think you're going?

472
00:24:40.820 --> 00:24:42.020
Don't move!

473
00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:44.760
Whoa, did you see that kick?

474
00:24:44.790 --> 00:24:46.990
He's not some
run-of-the-mill civilian!

475
00:24:50.060 --> 00:24:51.970
Come on, now.

476
00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.000
If you keep saying
things like that...

477
00:24:58.410 --> 00:24:59.710
...I'll blush.

478
00:24:59.740 --> 00:25:01.340
It wasn't a compliment!

479
00:25:01.340 --> 00:25:03.050
He's making fun of us!

480
00:25:03.050 --> 00:25:03.650
Hey!

481
00:25:03.650 --> 00:25:04.650
Go let Rob Lucci know

482
00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:07.250
that we've got a suspicious
intruder on board!

483
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:08.820
Wait a minute!

484
00:25:11.420 --> 00:25:13.890
This insignificant little
matter isn't something

485
00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:16.690
we need to bother CP9 with.

486
00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:19.980
No matter how violent
or unruly this man is,

487
00:25:20.020 --> 00:25:21.690
it won't do him any good.

488
00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:24.890
Because, in this car, you've
got... Whoa, it's smoky!

489
00:25:26.630 --> 00:25:30.970
<b>CP6 Intelligence Agent, Jerry
Karate Island Native</b>

490
00:25:27.340 --> 00:25:29.420
In this car, you've got me!

491
00:25:29.420 --> 00:25:30.970
Jerry!

492
00:25:36.070 --> 00:25:37.410
That's right.

493
00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.740
You're looking at the champion
on a South Blue island

494
00:25:39.920 --> 00:25:42.160
renowned for its martial arts.

495
00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:45.930
The undefeated Boxing Champion!

496
00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:48.260
I prefer karate.

497
00:25:50.130 --> 00:25:54.070
If you can handle my punches
then maybe I'll show you some!

498
00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:55.970
Easy!

499
00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:57.370
No need to overdo it!

500
00:25:57.420 --> 00:26:01.990
Jerry Aurora Flicker!

501
00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:03.860
Hey, Jerry!

502
00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:06.100
Your target's behind you!

503
00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:08.930
You're a sneaky one!

504
00:26:08.960 --> 00:26:09.910
Now, listen!

505
00:26:09.910 --> 00:26:11.850
Don't think you have me
at a disadvantage just

506
00:26:11.880 --> 00:26:16.280
because I'm so very tall and
this train car is so very tiny!

507
00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:17.880
This is the first time
I've ever talked to someone

508
00:26:17.920 --> 00:26:20.000
whose head is where
their crotch should be.

509
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.460
My boxing technique
is more effective

510
00:26:21.460 --> 00:26:23.360
in tight places like this!

511
00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:25.430
Prepare for annihilation!

512
00:26:25.490 --> 00:26:27.890
Go, Yoga Style!

513
00:26:27.930 --> 00:26:28.900
One-two!

514
00:26:28.930 --> 00:26:30.830
You just shortened your reach!

515
00:26:30.860 --> 00:26:31.990
That's what you think!

516
00:26:31.990 --> 00:26:33.390
All part of the plan.

517
00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:35.830
Screw!

518
00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:38.260
Drop Kick!

519
00:26:38.300 --> 00:26:41.770
That's totally against
every single rule of boxing!

520
00:26:41.800 --> 00:26:44.870
This is a waste of time.

521
00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:48.500
Brochette!

522
00:26:58.610 --> 00:27:00.780
I'll start with the seventh and last car.

523
00:27:00.810 --> 00:27:03.480
All of the World Government
officials are there.

524
00:27:06.380 --> 00:27:10.380
In order of increasing strength,
the fifth car is next.

525
00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:12.950
That car holds 40 marines
and the man who leads them,

526
00:27:13.090 --> 00:27:16.660
a Navy Headquarters Captain
and former knight named T-Bone.

527
00:27:16.680 --> 00:27:18.910
Next, in the 4th car,
we have Wanze,

528
00:27:18.940 --> 00:27:21.950
an accomplished martial artist
from Cipher Pol number 7

529
00:27:22.090 --> 00:27:25.030
who also happens to be
the head steward on this trip.

530
00:27:25.060 --> 00:27:28.760
Standing by in the 3rd car is
Nero, the newest member of CP9,

531
00:27:28.800 --> 00:27:30.800
and a force to be reckoned with.

532
00:27:44.080 --> 00:27:46.050
Anyway, though we
are escorting criminals,

533
00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:48.720
with government personnel
as trained and powerful

534
00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:49.790
as the ones I mentioned,

535
00:27:49.820 --> 00:27:52.590
we needn't worry about
the possibility of a raid.

536
00:27:52.620 --> 00:27:53.690
Our military might

537
00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:55.660
is represented
throughout this train.

538
00:27:59.830 --> 00:28:01.100
Straw Hat!

539
00:28:01.130 --> 00:28:03.000
Zoro!

540
00:28:03.030 --> 00:28:04.570
We're here to help!

541
00:28:05.040 --> 00:28:06.460
Come out!

542
00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:08.290
Where are you?!

543
00:28:09.620 --> 00:28:12.790
Mister Foreman, it must be
hard for you to even move.

544
00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:13.990
Maybe you should take a little break.

545
00:28:14.050 --> 00:28:14.950
Don't be stupid!

546
00:28:14.960 --> 00:28:15.820
This is nothing!

547
00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:16.990
Hurry up and find them!

548
00:28:17.030 --> 00:28:18.030
Yes, sir!

549
00:28:19.290 --> 00:28:21.720
Has anyone gone to
bring Iceburg up to speed?

550
00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:24.120
Two men went to
give him a report!

551
00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:33.020
Hey, where are you
going, Mr. Iceburg?

552
00:28:34.180 --> 00:28:35.680
Sir?

553
00:28:37.640 --> 00:28:38.760
Hey, Zoro!

554
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:39.960
Where are you?

555
00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:41.820
Answer us, Straw Hat!

556
00:28:42.580 --> 00:28:44.160
Luffy!

557
00:28:44.260 --> 00:28:45.330
Zoro! Luffy!

558
00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:46.760
Come on guys, answer me!

559
00:28:46.790 --> 00:28:48.660
Where the heck are you?

560
00:28:50.830 --> 00:28:52.260
What's that?

561
00:28:52.370 --> 00:28:53.070
Food, you say?

562
00:28:53.240 --> 00:28:54.080
Yes, that's right.

563
00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:54.750
We need meat.

564
00:28:54.790 --> 00:28:55.820
All the meat you can find.

565
00:28:56.060 --> 00:28:56.760
And hurry!

566
00:28:56.760 --> 00:28:59.930
We're running out of time!

567
00:28:59.960 --> 00:29:02.860
How did we end up being a couple
of errand boys for that girl?!

568
00:29:02.900 --> 00:29:03.870
We're not doing this for her!

569
00:29:03.870 --> 00:29:05.450
We're doing it for Paulie!

570
00:29:05.450 --> 00:29:06.850
He's so devoted to
that crazy woman,

571
00:29:06.890 --> 00:29:07.960
even after she dumped him!

572
00:29:08.070 --> 00:29:09.640
We've gotta give this our all!

573
00:29:09.640 --> 00:29:10.520
Yeah, you're right!

574
00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:11.720
Keep going!

575
00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:14.560
In any case, she
must be really hungry!

576
00:29:14.590 --> 00:29:16.760
She's still a growing girl!

577
00:29:16.790 --> 00:29:17.560
Right?

578
00:29:17.590 --> 00:29:18.700
I guess!

579
00:29:24.830 --> 00:29:25.900
It's no use.

580
00:29:29.540 --> 00:29:30.830
Rain.

581
00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:32.560
This is bad.

582
00:29:32.600 --> 00:29:35.100
The strong winds are
already interfering

583
00:29:35.130 --> 00:29:36.970
with my sense of smell.

584
00:29:49.410 --> 00:29:50.320
Man, I'm beat.

585
00:29:50.350 --> 00:29:52.380
It feels like we've been
calling for hours,

586
00:29:52.420 --> 00:29:54.050
but there's still no answer.

587
00:29:54.090 --> 00:29:55.100
You think that maybe they're...

588
00:29:55.100 --> 00:29:56.010
Don't be ridiculous!

589
00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:59.040
Just keep trying!

590
00:30:00.140 --> 00:30:01.780
Luffy, Zoro!

591
00:30:01.810 --> 00:30:04.150
Where in the world are you?

592
00:30:04.240 --> 00:30:06.840
There's no way that leopard guy took you
out.

593
00:30:08.010 --> 00:30:10.060
We finally know
why Robin left us

594
00:30:10.060 --> 00:30:12.360
and we need to do
something about it!

595
00:30:12.390 --> 00:30:14.860
Straw Hat, where are you?!

596
00:30:14.950 --> 00:30:15.990
Answer us!

597
00:30:16.020 --> 00:30:17.920
Please!

598
00:30:21.160 --> 00:30:22.300
Hang in there, Robin.

599
00:30:22.330 --> 00:30:23.200
Luffy and the rest of us

600
00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:25.880
are coming to save
you no matter what!

601
00:30:36.530 --> 00:30:37.630
What's going on here?

602
00:30:37.660 --> 00:30:39.060
Oh! Paulie!

603
00:30:39.100 --> 00:30:40.560
Quick, come see for yourself!

604
00:30:44.570 --> 00:30:46.970
The more the tide recedes,

605
00:30:47.010 --> 00:30:49.580
the bigger the
returning waves will be.

606
00:30:49.610 --> 00:30:52.150
If you pay attention
to the ebb of the tide,

607
00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:56.150
you can measure the
magnitude of the storm surge.

608
00:30:56.180 --> 00:30:57.240
I'm flying!

609
00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:58.340
Meow!

610
00:30:58.470 --> 00:31:00.470
And, if you
consider how much lower

611
00:31:00.470 --> 00:31:04.140
the water level's
going to be this year.

612
00:31:04.700 --> 00:31:05.400
Hey, Chimney!

613
00:31:05.400 --> 00:31:07.210
Take a look!

614
00:31:08.710 --> 00:31:09.410
Whoa!

615
00:31:09.410 --> 00:31:10.940
Amazing!

616
00:31:10.970 --> 00:31:13.200
Meow! Meow! Meow!

617
00:31:21.520 --> 00:31:24.360
It's almost as if the sea has dried up.

618
00:31:24.390 --> 00:31:28.190
I haven't seen anything like this in my
entire life.

619
00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:31.340
The power of the sea is astonishing.

620
00:31:35.130 --> 00:31:36.330
No way.

621
00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:38.600
How can the tide be so low?

622
00:31:38.630 --> 00:31:41.870
I've never seen
anything like it!

623
00:31:42.540 --> 00:31:46.380
Just how big of a wave
is coming this time?

624
00:31:46.410 --> 00:31:50.450
All of the backstreets are going
to be completely swallowed up!

625
00:31:50.480 --> 00:31:52.220
I hope nobody's still down there.

626
00:31:52.250 --> 00:31:55.250
If there is,
they'll die instantly!

627
00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:04.010
The roar of the ocean.

628
00:32:04.050 --> 00:32:06.550
It's gone.

629
00:32:06.580 --> 00:32:08.520
Look-ee, look-ee,
look-ee, look-ee, look-ee!

630
00:32:08.550 --> 00:32:10.090
Meow, meow, meow!

631
00:32:10.120 --> 00:32:11.020
Hey, Granny!

632
00:32:11.050 --> 00:32:11.980
Take a look over there!

633
00:32:11.980 --> 00:32:13.350
I see something!

634
00:32:13.380 --> 00:32:15.720
You do, do you?

635
00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:16.720
Yeah!

636
00:32:16.720 --> 00:32:18.620
There's something between those two
buildings!

637
00:32:19.560 --> 00:32:20.860
Come on, Granny!

638
00:32:20.890 --> 00:32:22.360
Look! Look!

639
00:32:24.300 --> 00:32:25.630
Kokoro!

640
00:32:26.010 --> 00:32:26.710
Oh!

641
00:32:26.740 --> 00:32:29.080
If it isn't the pirate girl!

642
00:32:29.110 --> 00:32:29.850
Hey!

643
00:32:29.930 --> 00:32:31.400
Miss Pirate Lady!

644
00:32:31.400 --> 00:32:31.920
Look!

645
00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:33.050
Look over there!

646
00:32:33.080 --> 00:32:35.480
I see something!

647
00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:37.350
Like what?

648
00:32:37.760 --> 00:32:41.060
Just what are you going on about,
Chimney?

649
00:32:41.090 --> 00:32:42.460
No way!

650
00:32:42.490 --> 00:32:44.000
What happened to the sea?

651
00:32:44.030 --> 00:32:45.600
It's dried up!

652
00:32:54.290 --> 00:32:56.080
Luffy!

653
00:32:57.330 --> 00:32:59.460
That straw hat.

654
00:32:59.960 --> 00:33:02.960
Isn't that your "King
of the Pirates" captain?

655
00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:05.360
Well?

656
00:33:06.530 --> 00:33:08.430
That idiot!

657
00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:11.700
Hey, hold on!

658
00:33:11.730 --> 00:33:13.340
Where do you think you're going?

659
00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:14.670
Don't go down
to the back streets!

660
00:33:14.700 --> 00:33:15.680
It's dangerous!

661
00:33:15.680 --> 00:33:17.320
Are you trying
to kill yourself?!

662
00:33:17.350 --> 00:33:21.390
Aqua Laguna is gonna hit
at any moment! Come back!

663
00:33:25.010 --> 00:33:26.910
The pirate girl went down the stairs!

664
00:33:26.950 --> 00:33:28.580
What should we do?

665
00:33:28.620 --> 00:33:29.320
Come back!

666
00:33:29.350 --> 00:33:31.150
What if another wave hits?!
